WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:04.920
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.240
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.520
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:08.760
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.580
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:19.580
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:20.720
We're The Office Ladies.

8
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:24.680
Hi!

9
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:25.800
Hello, miss.

10
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:26.500
How are you?

11
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:27.520
I'm good.

12
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.440
I'm good, too.

13
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.820
I didn't sleep great last night, but I have a weird amount of energy.

14
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.320
I think we're in the loopy zone because I have the same thing.

15
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.120
All right.

16
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.940
Well, today, we're going to be talking about Moving On, Part 2.

17
00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:48.480
It is Season 9, Episode 17, written by Graham Wagner and directed by Jon Favreau.

18
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.440
Here is your summary.

19
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:57.420
Andy retaliates against Aaron and Pete by summoning their exes to the office under false pretenses.

20
00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:58.600
Mm-hmm.

21
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.000
Toby is going to finally confront the convicted Scranton Strangler.

22
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.640
He wants to tell them, I think you're innocent.

23
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:12.940
Pam makes a decision about her future in Philly, and Dwight and Angela have a special moment of connection while caring for Aunt Shirley.

24
00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.920
And now, I have some news that I could not be more excited to share.

25
00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.840
I'm telling you, if you build it up too much, it's going to disappoint.

26
00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:27.480
Everybody, Angela is doing our top of show today.

27
00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.840
Yes, because last week, we talked all about Moving On, Part 1.

28
00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:33.220
We did our fast facts.

29
00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:33.880
We did.

30
00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.660
We did some of our call sheet tidbits.

31
00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.440
So, Jenna was like, Ange, you want to have a go at top of show?

32
00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.380
And you guys?

33
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:43.380
Okay.

34
00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.540
I think it's going to be a really fun, fresh energy for you to do top of show.

35
00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.040
Okay, well, I have a surprise for you.

36
00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:49.800
What is it?

37
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.140
I will lead with this.

38
00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:52.320
I have two surprises.

39
00:01:52.660 --> 00:02:01.100
First of all, did you know that there was a card on the writer's room wall, remember their wall of ideas, that said ski trip?

40
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:03.320
No, I did not.

41
00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:04.720
Yes, there was.

42
00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.900
I did confer with Warren about this.

43
00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.760
And, you know, Jenna, we have been so fortunate from our writer's assistants to get all of the scripts.

44
00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:18.060
I did find a pitch for ski trip.

45
00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.360
You did not.

46
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.080
I did.

47
00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:27.880
Apparently, Andy can't stand being inside all day and announces he wants to go on a staff ski trip at the end of the week.

48
00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:30.160
Dwight thinks it's a waste of time.

49
00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:35.940
Andy says that they have enough discretionary funds for ski lift passes.

50
00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.500
There's a deal online, and the whole bullpen is very excited about it.

51
00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:45.520
And apparently, Angela used to be a competitive skier, question mark.

52
00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:53.520
And then the other thing in the outline said simply this, Kevin in a ski school class.

53
00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.640
Oh, so Kevin's going to take ski school during this episode?

54
00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:57.950
Possibly.

55
00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:02.240
Like, there were so many ideas pitched off of this one card that just said ski trip.

56
00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:08.240
It just cracked me up thinking about the possibilities if our show ever really traveled anywhere.

57
00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:12.740
I think they should not put us all on skis.

58
00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.480
I mean, how many of us even know how to ski?

59
00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:16.920
I didn't know how to ski then.

60
00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:20.280
I mean, also, look at what happened on Work Bus.

61
00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:21.260
Exactly.

62
00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.680
You're going to put us on a mountain?

63
00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.080
No way.

64
00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.800
Anyway, it got me so tickled.

65
00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:34.040
And then surprise number two is this ski storyline made me think of how I only journal when I travel.

66
00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.540
And guess what?

67
00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:36.080
What?

68
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:44.820
I'm going to read you some travel journal entries from my journal from 2004, and it includes a ski trip.

69
00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.760
Oh, my gosh.

70
00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.800
You need to do top of show more often.

71
00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.100
I don't know about that.

72
00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.520
This is what I'm saying.

73
00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:55.400
These are delicious, delicious, delicious nuggets.

74
00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:56.180
Okay.

75
00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.700
I'm getting my journal.

76
00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.200
Look at all my Post-it notes.

77
00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.540
Look at them where I've marked these entries.

78
00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:02.000
Okay.

79
00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:04.120
Here goes.

80
00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.100
I apologize in advance.

81
00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:12.340
October 19th, 2004, 4.10 p.m.

82
00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:12.820
Tuesday.

83
00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.560
I love how you put the time.

84
00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:15.140
I know.

85
00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.780
This journal entry is from the set of The Office.

86
00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.700
I'm in the background of a scene.

87
00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:22.060
This is our last—

88
00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.580
By the way, I want to say, that's not you setting up this journal.

89
00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:25.400
That's what you wrote.

90
00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:25.640
Yes.

91
00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:25.920
Right?

92
00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:26.260
Mm-hmm.

93
00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:27.420
This journal entry.

94
00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:27.840
Oh, I love it.

95
00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.120
This journal entry is from the set of The Office.

96
00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.540
I'm in the background of a scene.

97
00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:34.580
This is our last week of work, at least for now.

98
00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:38.220
I so, underline, hope we get picked up.

99
00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.560
Lord, please let us get picked up.

100
00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:46.040
NBC was maybe going to pay for an extra episode, and we were going to shoot it next week, but

101
00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.940
they decided not to at the last minute.

102
00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.520
We're all pretty bummed.

103
00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.800
I'm sad, but at the same time, I'm happy because I'm going to go see my mom and dad

104
00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:54.340
in Texas.

105
00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:58.580
Oh, Oscar just drew a Post-it note, and then I added on to it.

106
00:04:58.740 --> 00:04:59.440
Here it is.

107
00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.740
And then you put the Post-it in your journal.

108
00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:09.120
It's like me, if I was a monkey dressed as Angela Martin, and then I added the monkey

109
00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.160
pooping, and then Oscar wrote, Touché!

110
00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:12.780
Well played.

111
00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.780
Was that season one?

112
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:15.320
Yes.

113
00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:15.970
2004?

114
00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:16.760
Yes.

115
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:17.700
Oh, my gosh.

116
00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:18.200
Okay.

117
00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.060
Now is my trip.

118
00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:20.920
Okay.

119
00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.240
Next entry.

120
00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.600
October 25th, 2004.

121
00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.240
Monday, 1.15 p.m.

122
00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:30.120
On American Airlines, headed to Dallas, then on to Wichita Falls.

123
00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:38.340
It is an international plane, so I have my own TV with 10 channels of stuff to watch,

124
00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:46.500
five movie channels, and then ESPN, News Channel, Cartoon Network, and the BBC.

125
00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.840
Oh, boy.

126
00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:50.240
Just bought headsets.

127
00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.060
$2, but worth it.

128
00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.680
No movies on yet, so I'm listening to classical music.

129
00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:57.520
Very soothing.

130
00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.520
Boeing 777.

131
00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:05.940
These are, what are these ridiculous?

132
00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:09.640
You start just describing, like, your literal surroundings.

133
00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:10.200
Ridiculous.

134
00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:10.740
Okay, ready?

135
00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:11.220
Yes.

136
00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:13.880
Watched Chronicles of Riddick.

137
00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.940
Little stupid, but okay.

138
00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.100
I guess for an in-flight movie.

139
00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.640
So, I think I'm going to miss my connecting flight to Wichita Falls.

140
00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:23.320
We'll see.

141
00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:24.740
It's going to be super tight.

142
00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:30.040
And then I say, we land at 6 p.m., and my flight leaves at 6.49 p.m.

143
00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:34.180
I get in at gate A21 and have to go all the way to A2.

144
00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:35.020
Ugh.

145
00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:36.320
Did you write that?

146
00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:36.860
Ugh.

147
00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:41.540
And then my next entry says, midnight in Archer City, Texas.

148
00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.120
I'm in the guest room.

149
00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:43.940
Unbelievable.

150
00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:45.500
I made my connecting flight.

151
00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.000
And so did my luggage.

152
00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.000
Amazing, really.

153
00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:53.620
Here's what I want everybody out there to know, is that that journal entry that you just read

154
00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:58.080
could very easily be an audio memo that you left me.

155
00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.920
Like, those are the details that I get.

156
00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:01.400
I know.

157
00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.500
I get the nitty-gritty.

158
00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:08.340
You would, in your audio memo to me, you would probably list out all of the different

159
00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:09.580
channels that are available.

160
00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:13.060
Then, now I'm in Texas, right?

161
00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:18.880
And I wrote, we surprised grandmother with a new stove, and she showed us the 250-foot

162
00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:21.680
sprint sail tower that they built behind her house.

163
00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:24.140
She's oddly and sweetly very proud of it.

164
00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:25.840
She took a ton of pictures of it.

165
00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:27.020
I'm frightened by it.

166
00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:29.780
Oh, my God.

167
00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:32.840
And now the last one is the ski story.

168
00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:33.320
Ready?

169
00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:38.120
January 1st, Salt Lake City to San Francisco to LAX.

170
00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:38.560
Ah!

171
00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:41.300
Oh, my gosh.

172
00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:41.740
Why?

173
00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:42.980
Why were you so upset about this?

174
00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:43.700
So many connections.

175
00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:44.460
So many connections.

176
00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:45.580
Very tired.

177
00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:46.840
Have a crick in my neck.

178
00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.400
And I'm so ready for my bed.

179
00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:49.740
I miss my home.

180
00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.540
And, of course, Lucy and Otter, my cats.

181
00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.740
The cabin was very cozy.

182
00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:57.720
We got in at midnight on the 28th, and it was snowing.

183
00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:59.900
And it didn't stop the whole time we were there.

184
00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.760
It was literally a snowstorm.

185
00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.140
It even made the national news.

186
00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:04.900
Okay.

187
00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:08.220
I took a snowboarding class on the worst day of the storm.

188
00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.740
Typical frowny face.

189
00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:11.200
Aw!

190
00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.500
Just your luck.

191
00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:15.220
Womp, womp.

192
00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.540
It was a blizzard out there.

193
00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.120
I quit half an hour.

194
00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:24.690
Half an hour left.

195
00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:28.150
Everyone else met me in the cafe at 1230 p.m.

196
00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:30.230
I was on my second cup of Earl Grey.

197
00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:31.190
No regrets.

198
00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:35.740
I was miserably cold.

199
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:40.220
And you couldn't see three feet down the mountain for the gusts of wind and snow.

200
00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:41.760
And it just burned through me.

201
00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:43.140
I didn't dress warm enough.

202
00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:43.760
Ick.

203
00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:50.260
Now I'm in the window seat of a three-seat row flying home.

204
00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:54.200
The flight is pretty packed, and the guy in front of me has his seat back, and I seriously

205
00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:54.900
feel trapped.

206
00:08:55.220 --> 00:09:00.520
Of course, everyone else has put their seat up because we are landing, but not this jack-off

207
00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:01.260
in front of me.

208
00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.760
I wonder why I keep a journal.

209
00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:08.660
I mean, I only write in it when we travel.

210
00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:12.120
It's almost just a way for me to kill time on a plane, I guess.

211
00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.640
Oh, I think yes.

212
00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:14.420
I think yes.

213
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.240
Here are things I'd like to do, semicolon.

214
00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:18.680
Write a book or screenplay.

215
00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:23.080
Edit my pilot presentation for the show I'm writing about my hometown in Texas.

216
00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.080
Do another one-woman show.

217
00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:26.240
Learn to cook.

218
00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.220
Learn to speak Spanish more fluently.

219
00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:29.720
Work on my tennis game.

220
00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:30.820
I like that.

221
00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.680
Like, all of a sudden, you turned your journal into, like, a journal.

222
00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:35.020
Okay.

223
00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:36.920
Like, processing and goal-making.

224
00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:37.880
Last entry.

225
00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.940
Not that your other journal wasn't awesome.

226
00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:45.240
The lady next to the guy who won't pull his seat up is now telling him a story about her

227
00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.200
New Year's Eve in London.

228
00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:48.100
Apparently, there was a mob scene.

229
00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.480
Very festive and scary.

230
00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:52.040
Things I'd like to do continued.

231
00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:53.820
Just go straight into it.

232
00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:55.000
Get in shape.

233
00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:57.000
Seriously, though, I say that all the time.

234
00:09:57.420 --> 00:10:00.000
Oh, my God, she's still talking to him about London.

235
00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:00.920
Ha, ha, ha.

236
00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.140
Oh, my God, she's still talking.

237
00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:07.020
Gotta run, although writing in this is protecting me from chatty patty.

238
00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:07.820
Wow.

239
00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:08.640
There you go.

240
00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:09.500
I loved it.

241
00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.760
And I want to say something.

242
00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:15.560
Those things that you wrote down in your journal, almost all of them have manifested now.

243
00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:18.460
I mean, I know it's been a long passage of time.

244
00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:18.800
A long time, yeah.

245
00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:23.520
But it's, I feel like the only one is you never did another one-woman show.

246
00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.360
No, and that's okay with me.

247
00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:25.720
Yeah.

248
00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:26.080
Yeah.

249
00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:27.460
But, wow.

250
00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:34.440
I mean, just goes to show you guys, just hang in there for 40 years and a list you make on an airplane.

251
00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:35.460
All right.

252
00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:39.200
I have no idea if that was interesting to you all, but there's my top of show.

253
00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.980
Inspired by a card on the writer's room wall.

254
00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:43.400
I beyond loved it.

255
00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:47.620
Everyone, please vote if you would like Angela to do more Top of Show.

256
00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:48.500
Please don't.

257
00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:49.520
Please don't.

258
00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:50.720
All right.

259
00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.960
We're going to take a break and we will be back to finish breaking down.

260
00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:54.620
Moving on.

261
00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:55.200
Part two.

262
00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:12.890
This episode is going to officially open with Dwight and Angela bathing Aunt Shirley.

263
00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:15.230
Quote bathing in quotes.

264
00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:15.950
Yeah.

265
00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:22.330
I mean, Dwight shows Angela the bathing area and it's basically Aunt Shirley sitting in a chair

266
00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:28.210
and Angela has a giant fire hose and she ends up spraying Dwight with it.

267
00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:28.790
Mm-hmm.

268
00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.210
We had a fan question from Ludovica F.

269
00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.650
from Zurich who said,

270
00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:39.070
When Angela hoses down Dwight, we see rain reaching down to protect his jewels.

271
00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:40.570
Did that hurt him?

272
00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:43.990
Can you tell us all about this scene and how many takes it took to do this?

273
00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:45.070
Angela?

274
00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:49.610
Ludovica, thank you so much for that question because I have lots of stuff to share.

275
00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:54.090
First of all, we had a hose rehearsal earlier in the week.

276
00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:58.350
Yeah, Steve Burgess told me you did that, that you did the rehearsal on Monday.

277
00:11:58.610 --> 00:11:59.810
You shot this on Thursday.

278
00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:03.230
I wasn't clear if you were also at the hose rehearsal.

279
00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.710
Yes, I was because I had to hold the hose.

280
00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:06.050
Okay.

281
00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:10.010
So they had these fellas that were showing me how to use it.

282
00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:15.110
And I was told that the hose was set to a much lower pressure than it would normally be on

283
00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:19.050
because if it was turned all the way on, it would probably lift me off the ground.

284
00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:20.070
Oh, my gosh.

285
00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:20.550
Yeah.

286
00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:26.690
They also told me that I really had to try to make sure not to aim at Rain's face

287
00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:33.370
because even at a lower setting, this water hose to the eyeball could result in a corneal abrasion

288
00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:34.830
or an eye contusion.

289
00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:35.670
Oh, my gosh.

290
00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:37.970
So you aim low, aim low.

291
00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:38.590
Aim low.

292
00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:40.110
They told me, aim low.

293
00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:43.330
They gave me like an area on Rain's body.

294
00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:47.010
It was basically like ribcage to knees to try to aim for.

295
00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.510
And it was a good thing he wore glasses.

296
00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:52.310
They thought that was helpful.

297
00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:53.970
I have a question.

298
00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:55.830
Was Rain at the rehearsal or just you?

299
00:12:56.350 --> 00:13:00.850
Rain was at the rehearsal too because I had to kind of practice a little bit.

300
00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:01.190
Okay.

301
00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:04.830
And even at the lower pressure, it was a lot to handle.

302
00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.610
You sort of see me struggling with it.

303
00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:08.490
That's a little bit of acting, but a little bit not.

304
00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:11.790
Like, I didn't have really great aim with it.

305
00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:15.310
So I was glad Rain was tall and I had a bigger target.

306
00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:18.050
Oh, Creed just tried to call me.

307
00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:18.790
Oh.

308
00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:20.010
I have a missed call from Creed.

309
00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.130
Oh, Creed has his new album out.

310
00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:23.690
Oh, yes, he does.

311
00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:24.550
Oh, my gosh.

312
00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:25.450
And he's going on tour.

313
00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:26.970
Should I call and ask what he wanted?

314
00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:27.510
Sure.

315
00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:28.070
Okay.

316
00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:33.350
Hello, pumpkin.

317
00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:34.610
Hey, Credo.

318
00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:35.750
I'm here with Jenna.

319
00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:38.170
We were doing our podcast when you called.

320
00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.050
Oh, you're on the show right now.

321
00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:40.910
You stopped it, I hope.

322
00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:42.270
No, no, you're on.

323
00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:42.950
You're on.

324
00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:48.910
We're excited about your new album.

325
00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.470
You're hitting the road, aren't you?

326
00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:58.070
I'm going to Europe in October, but the album comes out September 27th.

327
00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.110
Oh, fun.

328
00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:01.570
And the shameless promotion, ladies, thank you so much.

329
00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:02.370
There you go.

330
00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:03.970
Well, I miss you.

331
00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.930
Were you just calling to say hey?

332
00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:10.670
Yeah, I was calling to say hey, and I actually was going to ask you what season you are on.

333
00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:11.350
I was just curious.

334
00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:13.830
Oh, we're on season nine, Creed.

335
00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:15.210
Oh, my God.

336
00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:16.930
You're getting close to the finale.

337
00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:17.850
We are.

338
00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:19.510
You'll have to come on.

339
00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.330
I want everyone to come on for the finale.

340
00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:22.050
Me too.

341
00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:25.730
I should come on and actually bring my guitar to me on the basis.

342
00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:27.110
Come on.

343
00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:29.350
Creed, I would love that.

344
00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:30.450
We would love it.

345
00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.710
Not a dry eye in the house.

346
00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:33.450
Nope.

347
00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:36.810
It was so good to see you on the AT&T thing.

348
00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:38.850
It had been so long.

349
00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:39.730
I know.

350
00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.330
We got to work together again.

351
00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:42.270
It was so amazing.

352
00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:43.470
How cute is that?

353
00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.710
Well, I miss you so much.

354
00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.370
We need to go for our neighborhood walk.

355
00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:48.950
We need to do that.

356
00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:50.450
Call me later.

357
00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:52.970
And now, Creed, tell us when your single comes out.

358
00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.870
June 24th, Corner of the Universe.

359
00:14:55.870 --> 00:15:01.010
I wrote it with Vance DeGeneres, you know, who used to run Steve's company.

360
00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:02.430
That is amazing.

361
00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:04.170
Creed, this is crazy.

362
00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:05.610
You're calling today.

363
00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:09.290
We're recording this episode, and it's like perfect timing.

364
00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:12.450
Your single is out right now when this airs.

365
00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.290
The single will be out when this airs, yes.

366
00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:14.750
Yes.

367
00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:17.850
Everyone, check out Creed's new single.

368
00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:19.490
Creed, tell us the name of it again.

369
00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:20.950
Corner of the Universe.

370
00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:22.290
Corner of the Universe.

371
00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:23.610
I can't wait to hear it.

372
00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:25.930
We're going to play a little of it at the end of this episode.

373
00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:30.130
And then, Creed, we'll put little swipe-ups and stuff so folks can find it.

374
00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:31.310
And I'm so glad you called.

375
00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:31.890
I miss you.

376
00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:33.010
That's perfect.

377
00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:34.910
Well, my ears were burning.

378
00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:38.330
I just got back from having a gluten-free muffin, and all of a sudden, I was going,

379
00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:39.710
call Angela and Jen.

380
00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:42.310
Really, I just picked up the phone and said, well, all right.

381
00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:43.630
My voice says, call them.

382
00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:43.970
I will.

383
00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:44.630
And there you go.

384
00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:45.430
That's how it works.

385
00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:47.070
Oh, we love you, Creed.

386
00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:47.770
Love you, Creed.

387
00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:49.530
I'll see you soon in the neighborhood.

388
00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:50.530
All right.

389
00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:50.970
Bye.

390
00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:55.350
Like, that's crazy.

391
00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:56.470
That is crazy.

392
00:15:56.610 --> 00:16:00.150
That's so, like, that is just serendipity right there.

393
00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:01.070
You know what that is?

394
00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:05.230
That's that thing that you talked about that we have as a cast, that, like, group mind.

395
00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:05.890
The group mind.

396
00:16:05.890 --> 00:16:08.870
We are connected as we just really are connected.

397
00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:09.530
We are.

398
00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:12.310
You know, I just am so thankful for it.

399
00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:17.550
I feel like I hear from someone in the cast or from you just at that moment when I needed it.

400
00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:20.770
And I just love that Creed called.

401
00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:21.930
I had my ringer off.

402
00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:22.730
I wouldn't have seen it.

403
00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:27.330
But I had just picked up my phone to play Rain's audio clip and saw that Creed had called.

404
00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:31.890
Well, you know, when we did the commercial together, he said he had his new album coming

405
00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:32.130
out.

406
00:16:32.230 --> 00:16:35.890
And I said, will you call us and let us know when that single drops?

407
00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.010
Because we want to talk about it on Office Ladies.

408
00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:40.550
And then he just called, like.

409
00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:41.730
While we're recording.

410
00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:43.230
I just can't get over it.

411
00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.130
The universe is a beautiful place.

412
00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:46.010
Okay.

413
00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:47.030
Well, now, where was I?

414
00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:49.350
You were about to play the Rain audio clip.

415
00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:51.610
I was about to play a Rain audio clip.

416
00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:57.190
So yesterday, I texted Rain and I said, hey, tall fella, random question for you.

417
00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:00.750
Did it hurt you when I sprayed you with that fire hose and moving on?

418
00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:03.310
A few people noted I hit your crotch.

419
00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:04.650
I mean, it was a fire hose.

420
00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:05.410
I'm so sorry.

421
00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:10.710
And then I filmed the scene and I sent him the scene.

422
00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:14.890
And I told him, I said, I did remember they told me not to spray your face.

423
00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:17.010
And here is Rain's response.

424
00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:29.830
Hey, and that is one of the scenes I had completely forgotten that we had shot.

425
00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:34.070
And I forgot that that had existed.

426
00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:39.180
Now I remember filming it.

427
00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:40.580
It didn't hurt at all.

428
00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:41.440
I don't know.

429
00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:45.140
Maybe that giant plastic apron I had on.

430
00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:47.160
It didn't hurt my crotch or anything.

431
00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:54.100
But I imagine if you had blasted me in the face, that's what she said, that it would have hurt a great deal.

432
00:17:54.100 --> 00:18:01.720
But I remember that being very super fun and funny now.

433
00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:03.700
And thank you for the little reminder.

434
00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:07.100
But I have no other memories.

435
00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:14.100
Crazy.

436
00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:15.920
All right.

437
00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:17.940
Well, there you have it.

438
00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.080
It did not hurt him.

439
00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:22.760
I did by accident get the sight of his ear one time.

440
00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:24.080
I do remember that.

441
00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:27.980
And I remember him after the next take saying, don't get my ear.

442
00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:30.740
And I was like, I didn't mean to get your ear.

443
00:18:32.060 --> 00:18:40.320
But the other thing I want to tell you is that several crew members came up to me and said that was the best part of their day.

444
00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:42.280
Was watching you hose rain?

445
00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:42.900
Yes.

446
00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:49.840
Well, Steve Burgess said that he doesn't remember how many takes you had to do, but it was more than one.

447
00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:50.820
Oh, it was.

448
00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:51.080
Yeah.

449
00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:59.020
He also said that all of Aunt Shirley's house for this episode was at the Warner Brothers Ranch, which you shared last week.

450
00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:04.940
But he said this barn where you did the hosing was the barn from the Waltons.

451
00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:05.880
Yes.

452
00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:07.780
The Warner Brothers Ranch is huge.

453
00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:15.580
So where we filmed the house, which was near the Friends Fountain, you know, we talked about that last week, was a totally different part of this ranch.

454
00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:20.080
And the barn is, like, kind of back where they had more of the Old West stuff.

455
00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:27.340
And I do want you guys to know, of course, Rain told me to go for it because I was like, I don't know.

456
00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:27.700
I'm scared.

457
00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:29.500
He was like, just hose me.

458
00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:30.520
I was like, okay.

459
00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:35.860
And this scene was longer in the shooting draft, and we did shoot it.

460
00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:37.840
It had one extra beat.

461
00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:40.900
After I yell at them and say, do you have a bathtub?

462
00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:42.120
And Dwight's like, yes.

463
00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:43.100
And then I'm like, good.

464
00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:45.320
It would have continued one more beat.

465
00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:47.760
In the shooting draft, it read like this.

466
00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:50.780
Angela drops the hose and marches inside.

467
00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:53.860
Aunt Shirley says to Dwight, feisty one.

468
00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:58.040
And Dwight, titillated, says, yes, she is.

469
00:19:58.460 --> 00:19:58.880
Hmm.

470
00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:02.480
Well, that leads me into this fan question from Joanne M.

471
00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:04.680
from Calgary, Alberta, Canada, who said,

472
00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:08.740
I love the side of Angela that we get to see in these episodes.

473
00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:13.180
She might be intolerant and bitchy, but she's a strong woman.

474
00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.500
She does not put up with crap.

475
00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:21.000
And I want to know how Angela felt about this new side of her character being highlighted.

476
00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:23.200
She's awesome in this one.

477
00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.240
Oh, Joanne, thank you.

478
00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:27.340
I just had so much fun.

479
00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:31.180
You know, we'd all been playing these characters for a long time.

480
00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:37.620
And whenever we got to show a new side of them or a new layer, it was like the first day all over again.

481
00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:38.020
Mm-hmm.

482
00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:39.060
That kind of excitement.

483
00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:40.880
So I was so tickled.

484
00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:41.640
I don't know.

485
00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.600
I liked her so much in this.

486
00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:44.840
Yeah, I did, too.

487
00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:45.740
I did, too.

488
00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:53.520
So next up, Toby's at the water cooler, and he is still talking to Nellie, rehashing details of the Scranton Strangler case.

489
00:20:53.740 --> 00:20:56.160
Yeah, he's kind of trying to flirt with her.

490
00:20:56.320 --> 00:21:04.200
And if I had a Dundee for Toby, it would be called, worst pickup line goes to Toby Flinderson.

491
00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:05.800
You have to hear this.

492
00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:08.780
Hey, Nellie.

493
00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:10.180
Mm.

494
00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.120
I am so sick of February.

495
00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:17.100
It's the shortest month, but it sure doesn't feel that way.

496
00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:19.540
We should catch up.

497
00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:21.580
Wow.

498
00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:21.840
What?

499
00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:22.740
Why?

500
00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.920
He takes a sip of water and then goes, mm.

501
00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:25.900
Like, really?

502
00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.480
What is happening?

503
00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:30.740
Oh, man.

504
00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:32.340
February, huh?

505
00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:33.460
Like, what?

506
00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:42.740
Well, this storyline of Toby still investigating the Scranton Strangler case was originally shot for Couples Discount.

507
00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:49.160
We had cut this whole Toby runner from Couples Discount, and we had to put it in this episode to help make it an hour long.

508
00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:53.360
And Dave Rogers told us that this fit perfectly.

509
00:21:53.360 --> 00:21:55.980
Obviously, there was one thing that we had to shoot.

510
00:21:56.120 --> 00:22:05.440
We had to do a little pickup because Toby originally started this conversation with Nellie by asking if she wanted to go to the nail salon with him.

511
00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:07.680
But obviously, that wouldn't work here.

512
00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:10.740
So they shot your fancy pickup line instead, Angela.

513
00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:17.360
And Dave said, you can tell, if you look really closely, you can see that in the reshoot footage,

514
00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:22.680
Toby's hair is a little shorter because he had gotten a haircut between these two episodes.

515
00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:27.940
